{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>I bow down</b> — Some say: it is the sanctuary of Your holiness — the heavens, and this is far-fetched, on account of \"I bow down.\" The correct view: it is the place where the Ark was. We find in every book כל שמך with kamatz chataf; therefore the commentator who said כי הגדלת על כל with cholam is incorrect. It is a pausal form, and it lacks vav, like ואמרתך. And the correct view in my eyes: the revered Name has epithet-names, such as Adonai with kamatz gadol, also Elohim and El Shaddai. But the proper noun is what is written but not pronounced — it is the revered and awesome one above all. This Name was not known until our master Moses came, and HaShem said to him, this is that Name. And it is ואודה את שמך — which is the proper noun." "Now the meaning of כי הגדלת על כל — a Name that You have, namely the epithet-names, the revered Name that You have spoken."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 138, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:03.598747410Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}